    dct:description "Modern plate reconstructions make the spatial proposition explicit and strongly discriminating. Deep-time ocean-basin uncertainty remains, but existing data can clearly confirm or refute the broad stated inference." ;
    rdfs:comment "Proposed test with existing data: Reconstruct Silurian-to-present continental crust, ocean basins, and paleoshorelines from plate models and geological constraints. Quantify overlap between ancient and present continental and oceanic areas; extensive changes would refute rough positional continuity." ;
